# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Get information on an API key (v2) by its name. Requires API version `v3.12` or higher.

Unlike `wallix-bastion_apikey`, this v2 data source also exposes the `profile` and `description`
associated with the key.

## Example Usage

```terraform
# Get information about a specific API key (v2)
data "wallix-bastion_apikey_v2" "ci_pipeline" {
  apikey_name = "ci_pipeline"
}

# Use the profile to confirm the key's granted permissions
output "ci_pipeline_apikey_profile" {
  value = data.wallix-bastion_apikey_v2.ci_pipeline.profile
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### Lookup Key

`apikey_name` is the required lookup key. The data source returns an error if no v2 API key with
that name exists on the Bastion.

### API Version Requirement

This data source is only available with API version `v3.12` or higher. On older API versions,
use `wallix-bastion_apikey` instead.

### The `apikey` attribute

The Bastion API never returns the raw API key value — the `apikey` attribute always reads back
as a masked placeholder (`********`), whether read through this data source or the corresponding
`wallix-bastion_apikey_v2` resource. Use this data source to check metadata (name, profile,
description, IP limitation) about an existing key, not to retrieve its usable secret value.

### Profile

`profile` is the name of the profile associated with the key, determining what the key is
authorized to do when used against the REST API (e.g. `user`, `auditor`,
`system_administrator`).

### IP Limitation

`ip_limitation` is a comma-separated list of IP addresses allowed to use the key. An empty value
means the key can be used from any IP.
